 "final_summary": "The root cause was that the `_read_file` function in `tracker/config.py` failed to handle malformed JSON files, causing a JSONDecodeError during startup. The fix added proper exception handling for both OSError and json.JSONDecodeError, returning an empty dict in such cases to fall back to default configuration values. This ensures the API contract is respected and startup does not crash on malformed config files.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/config.py b/tracker/config.py\nindex d17fed6..0799872 100644\n--- a/tracker/config.py\n+++ b/tracker/config.py\n@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ def _read_file(path):\n     try:\n         with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n             data = json.load(handle)\n-    except OSError:\n+    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n         return {}\n     return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n \n",
